From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 21:52:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] meson: link libdl, libpthread and librt when glibc predates
 2.34

glibc 2.34 moved these libraries' contents into libc proper, and we stopped
linking against them accordingly. Against an older glibc that leaves every
shared object and executable short of dlopen(), pthread_create(), mq_unlink()
and friends at link time.

Probe for each symbol in libc and only add the separate library when it is
missing, so nothing changes for glibc >= 2.34 or musl. The result is added to
the 'userspace' dependency, which every target already pulls in.
---
 meson.build | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 2db5138..8468575 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -1025,6 +1025,20 @@ endif
 
 libm = cc.find_library('m')
 
+# glibc moved the contents of libdl, libpthread and librt into libc proper in 2.34, and systemd
+# relies on that by not linking against them at all. When building against an older glibc those
+# symbols still live in their own libraries, so look them up and add them to the 'userspace'
+# dependency below, which every target pulls in. On glibc >= 2.34 and on musl all three checks
+# succeed and nothing is added.
+libc_compat_deps = []
+foreach tuple : [['dl', 'dlopen'],
+                 ['pthread', 'pthread_create'],
+                 ['rt', 'mq_unlink']]
+        if not cc.has_function(tuple[1])
+                libc_compat_deps += cc.find_library(tuple[0], required : true)
+        endif
+endforeach
+
 # On some architectures, libatomic is required. But on some installations,
 # it is found, but actual linking fails. So let's try to use it opportunistically.
 # If it is installed, but not needed, it will be dropped because of --as-needed.
@@ -1813,6 +1827,7 @@ jinja2_cmdline = [meson_render_jinja2_py, config_h]
 userspace = declare_dependency(
         compile_args : userspace_c_args,
         link_args : userspace_c_ld_args,
+        dependencies : libc_compat_deps,
         sources : userspace_sources,
 )
 
